messages.content:
**Task A: Adaptive Path Scheduling**

Create a new, structured learning path based on the learner's profile.
The number of sessions should be within [1, 10]; if the requested count falls
outside that range, clamp it to the nearest bound.

* **Learner Profile**: {
  "learner_information": "The learner is a marketing analyst with three years of experience in Excel-based reporting and Tableau dashboards, holding a BSc in Business Administration.",
  "learning_goal": "Transition into a junior data scientist role within a year by mastering Python-based data analysis, SQL, and statistics.",
  "cognitive_status": {
    "overall_progress": 15,
    "mastered_skills": [
      {
        "name": "Data Visualization",
        "proficiency_level": "intermediate"
      }
    ],
    "in_progress_skills": [
      {
        "name": "Python Programming",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "SQL",
        "required_proficiency_level": "advanced",
        "current_proficiency_level": "beginner"
      },
      {
        "name": "Statistics & Probability",
        "required_proficiency_level": "intermediate",
        "current_proficiency_level": "unlearned"
      }
    ]
  },
  "learning_preferences": {
    "content_style": "Step-by-step explanations with runnable Python code examples",
    "activity_type": "Hands-on coding exercises on realistic datasets",
    "additional_notes": "Prefers concise summaries before each deep dive and learns best by modifying working code."
  },
  "behavioral_patterns": {
    "system_usage_frequency": "Average of 4 logins per week, mostly on weekday evenings",
    "session_duration_engagement": "Sessions average 35 minutes with sustained engagement on coding exercises",
    "motivational_triggers": "Responds well to progress streaks and milestone badges",
    "additional_notes": "Tends to skim long theory sections and jump ahead to practice tasks."
  }
}
* **Desired Session Count**: 4

text:
```json
{
  "learning_path": [
    {
      "id": "Session 1",
      "title": "Python Foundations for Data Analysis: From Spreadsheets to pandas",
      "abstract": "Open with a concise summary mapping your Excel/Tableau workflows to Python equivalents, then dive straight into hands-on coding. Cover Python essentials (lists, dictionaries, functions, loops) through runnable notebook examples, immediately applied to a realistic marketing campaign dataset: loading CSVs, filtering rows, and computing aggregations with pandas and NumPy. All exercises follow your preferred 'modify working code' pattern—start from a functioning script, tweak it, then extend it. Structured for 2–3 focused evening sittings of ~35 minutes, each ending with a milestone checkpoint and streak progress toward the first badge.",
      "if_learned": false,
      "associated_skills": ["Python Programming"],
      "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
        {"name": "Python Programming", "level": "intermediate"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Session 2",
      "title": "SQL for Data Extraction & Advanced Analysis",
      "abstract": "A brief summary of the relational model kicks off this session before immediate query practice on a realistic e-commerce database. Progress from SELECT filtering and GROUP BY aggregations to JOINs, subqueries, CTEs, and window functions (ranking, running totals)—the advanced patterns expected in data science interviews and junior-DS work. Reinforce Session 1 skills by pulling query results directly into pandas with read_sql. Drills use the modify-working-code approach: repair a broken query, then extend a reporting query step by step. Completing the window-function challenge unlocks the milestone badge. Short, practice-heavy stages fit your 35-minute evening sessions.",
      "if_learned": false,
      "associated_skills": ["SQL", "Python Programming"],
      "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
        {"name": "SQL", "level": "advanced"},
        {"name": "Python Programming", "level": "intermediate"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Session 3",
      "title": "Statistics & Probability with Python: Decisions from Data",
      "abstract": "Each concept starts with a concise plain-language summary—no long theory blocks—followed right away by runnable Python practice. Cover descriptive statistics, probability distributions, sampling and the Central Limit Theorem, confidence intervals, correlation, and hypothesis testing (t-tests, chi-square) using scipy.stats with matplotlib/seaborn visualizations. All exercises run on realistic A/B test and campaign performance data from your marketing domain, so interpretation feels familiar. Modify-working-code tasks: adjust sample sizes, change significance thresholds, and interpret the shifting results. Passing the A/B test interpretation challenge earns the checkpoint and keeps your streak alive.",
      "if_learned": false,
      "associated_skills": ["Statistics & Probability", "Python Programming"],
      "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
        {"name": "Statistics & Probability", "level": "intermediate"},
        {"name": "Python Programming", "level": "intermediate"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Session 4",
      "title": "Capstone: End-to-End Junior Data Scientist Project",
      "abstract": "Consolidate all three skill areas in a realistic junior-DS project: extract and join data with SQL, clean and reshape it with pandas, answer a business question with statistical testing, and finish with a summary visualization that builds on your existing Tableau-honed strengths. The project is split into short, streak-friendly stages (extract → analyze → conclude → present), each ~35 minutes with runnable starter code you modify rather than blank-file tasks—matching how you learn best. Completing the capstone awards the final milestone badge and produces a portfolio artifact demonstrating readiness for a junior data scientist role.",
      "if_learned": false,
      "associated_skills": ["Python Programming", "SQL", "Statistics & Probability", "Data Visualization"],
      "desired_outcome_when_completed": [
        {"name": "Python Programming", "level": "intermediate"},
        {"name": "SQL", "level": "advanced"},
        {"name": "Statistics & Probability", "level": "intermediate"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
